-- Iteration (SPEC §15): `Yield[T]` is an ordinary control effect. A function that performs it is a
-- generator: `fn range(lo: i32, hi: i32) -> 1 with Yield[i32]`, whose `yield(x)` passes `x` to
-- whoever runs it. Its one operation resumes and answers `()`, which makes it an iteration effect:
--
-- * `for x in range(1, 10) { … }` handles it: the body is the operation's clause, run at each
--   `yield`, and `break` or `return` cancels the rest of the generator, which drops what it holds;
-- * a call at a parameter of type `pull A B R`, or bound as one, is the generator stored: its
--   clause keeps the continuation, the next observation resumes it, and `close` cancels it.
--
-- A generator's loop is a loop of its body (`while`, `loop`, a `for` over a stored generator or an
-- iterator), one turn per observation; the operation is performed inside the turn.

effect Yield[T] { ctl yield(x: T) }
